Let $k$ be an infinite field and $S=k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ the standard graded polynomial ring. Fix integers $c,n\ge 1$ and consider homogeneous ideals $I\subset S$ generated by a tuple $U=(f_1,\dots,f_c)$ of quadratic forms, and set $R=S/I$. Fix integers $p,q$ and a homogeneous presentation matrix $V$ of size $p\times q$ with linear entries over $R$, defining a finitely generated graded $R$-module $M=\mathrm{coker}(V)$. The data $(U,V)$ is parametrized by a (smooth, irreducible) affine variety $X$ whose points are pairs consisting of $c$ quadratic forms in $S$ together with a $p\times q$ matrix of linear forms.

Consider the following two loci in $X$:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] $X_{\mathrm{const}} = \{(U,V)\in X : \text{the graded Betti numbers } \beta_{i,j}^{R}(\mathrm{coker}(V)) \text{ take a value independent of }(U,V) \text{ on }X_{\mathrm{const}}\}$;
\item[(b)] $X_{\mathrm{const,np}} = \{(U,V)\in X_{\mathrm{const}} : \text{the minimal graded free resolution of } \mathrm{coker}(V) \text{ over } R \text{ is not eventually periodic}\}$.
\end{itemize}

Question: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Does $X_{\mathrm{const}}$ contain a nonempty Zariski open subset of $X$?
\item Does $X_{\mathrm{const,np}}$ contain a nonempty Zariski open subset of $X$?
\end{enumerate}

